  "summary": {
    "en": "Ankylosaurus was a low, wide plant-eater covered in bony armour plates, with a heavy club at the end of its tail. It lived in western North America at the very end of the Cretaceous, alongside Tyrannosaurus and Triceratops. Although it is famous, it is known only from incomplete skeletons, so palaeontologists still estimate its full size from its relatives."
